{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/hotsite_guestentry

    The interstitial page of the hotsite's guest entry: what an anonymous visitor
    of the "enter as guest" address sees for the moment it takes to enter.

    One form, posting the session key and the entry field to the hotsite's own
    address. The module theme_dimensions/hotsiteguest submits it on
    load; the button is the same submission without JavaScript. The bar is
    decoration and hidden from assistive technology.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * formid - Id of the form, the module's handle on it.
    * action - The hotsite's own address, where the form posts.
    * field - Name of the field asking for the entry.
    * sesskey - The session key.
    * heading - The sentence naming the course being opened.
    * message - The sentence saying the visitor enters as a guest.
    * button - Text of the button.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "formid": "theme_dimensions-guestentry",
        "action": "https://example.org/theme_dimensions/hotsite/2",
        "field": "guestenter",
        "sesskey": "abcdef1234",
        "heading": "Opening “Risk management in dams”…",
        "message": "You are entering as a guest.",
        "button": "Enter now"
    }
}}
<div class="dimensions-guestentry">
    <div class="dimensions-guestentry__card">
        <h1 class="dimensions-guestentry__heading">{{heading}}</h1>
        <p class="dimensions-guestentry__message">{{message}}</p>
        <div class="dimensions-guestentry__bar" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
        <form id="{{formid}}" class="dimensions-guestentry__form" method="post" action="{{action}}">
            <input type="hidden" name="{{field}}" value="1">
            <input type="hidden" name="sesskey" value="{{sesskey}}">
            <button type="submit" class="btn dimensions-guestentry__button">{{button}}</button>
        </form>
    </div>
</div>
